WEBVTT

00:47.255 --> 00:48.173
<i>Me?</i>

00:50.175 --> 00:52.427
<i>No, me.</i>

00:53.553 --> 00:54.971
<i>It's me, for sure.</i>

00:55.805 --> 00:57.307
<i>Maybe it's me.</i>

00:57.932 --> 00:59.059
<i>Ought to be me.</i>

00:59.559 --> 01:00.810
<i>Hey! It's me.</i>

01:01.394 --> 01:02.520
<i>Me.</i>

01:02.604 --> 01:03.980
<i>Me, me, me.</i>

01:04.064 --> 01:05.356
<i>It's me.</i>

01:05.440 --> 01:06.357
<i>Me, of course.</i>

01:06.941 --> 01:08.485
<i>- It's me.
- Me, obviously.</i>

01:08.568 --> 01:09.944
<i>- Me!
- It's me.</i>

01:10.028 --> 01:12.030
<i>- Of course it's me.
- Me!</i>

01:27.879 --> 01:29.089
So, how goes it?

01:29.172 --> 01:33.051
If he were human, I'd say he's dreaming.

01:34.094 --> 01:37.013
But there's absolutely
no sign of him waking up.

01:38.264 --> 01:39.432
I see.

01:41.309 --> 01:43.228
You're better off not seeing his face.

01:43.895 --> 01:47.273
The 9.9 billion personalities
programmed in him

01:47.357 --> 01:52.362
are being simulated on his artificial skin
at an incredible speed.

01:53.655 --> 01:56.324
It's beyond imagination
how hideous his face would be.

01:58.034 --> 02:03.081
Perhaps it is impossible
to create a perfect robot after all.

02:04.499 --> 02:06.042
What should we do?

02:06.126 --> 02:07.710
How can we wake him up?

02:08.503 --> 02:10.797
There is a way.

02:11.297 --> 02:12.132
What?

02:12.674 --> 02:13.925
Are you prepared?

02:16.719 --> 02:19.139
He may turn out to be a devil.

02:23.268 --> 02:24.602
A devil, huh?

02:25.270 --> 02:26.396
Dr. Tenma.

02:28.815 --> 02:30.692
She went back to her country.

02:31.776 --> 02:32.652
"She"?

02:33.153 --> 02:35.864
Gesicht's wife. Helena.

02:35.947 --> 02:36.990
I see.

02:37.657 --> 02:39.659
I wish you could have met her.

02:41.703 --> 02:44.539
She was concerned about Atom.

02:46.040 --> 02:47.792
Though it pains me to admit,

02:47.876 --> 02:52.463
we scientists tend to focus
only on technological results,

02:53.089 --> 02:56.759
but her sense of kindness
is worth studying too.

02:57.635 --> 02:58.678
It's almost as if

02:59.304 --> 03:01.931
she were Atom's equal.

03:06.519 --> 03:07.687
Dr. Tenma.

03:08.396 --> 03:12.066
The National Diet has set the date
for Atom's state funeral.

03:23.786 --> 03:28.917
With that, Gesicht's death
won't be in vain, right?

03:31.336 --> 03:34.881
We humans call things like this
"a soul" as well.

03:35.840 --> 03:38.801
I will take good care of
your husband's soul.

03:42.931 --> 03:45.642
<i>You are entering
a Class-A restricted zone.</i>

03:46.142 --> 03:47.852
<i>Retinal scan in progress.</i>

03:52.482 --> 03:53.858
<i>Please proceed.</i>

03:59.989 --> 04:01.783
<i>Devil or not, it doesn't matter!</i>

04:01.866 --> 04:04.535
Nothing matters unless he wakes up.

04:05.036 --> 04:06.246
What do we do?

04:08.039 --> 04:10.708
Introduce unbalanced emotions.

04:11.793 --> 04:14.587
"Unbalanced emotions"?

04:15.129 --> 04:20.051
Yes. Anger, sorrow, hatred...

04:20.843 --> 04:25.431
Tipping the scale is the simplest way
to solve the chaos of 9.9 billion.

04:37.986 --> 04:40.822
To bring you back from the dead,

04:41.572 --> 04:43.783
I'd gladly become a devil.

04:56.754 --> 04:58.339
Gesicht's hatred...

05:00.758 --> 05:04.387
As Gesicht... died...

05:07.640 --> 05:09.809
toward whom was he directing his hatred?

05:14.480 --> 05:17.442
It's been raining for three days.

05:19.110 --> 05:21.612
At this rate, just like Gesicht, I might...

05:22.655 --> 05:25.908
Epsilon, you have a visitor.
He looks really strong.

05:30.079 --> 05:31.581
It sure rains a lot here.

05:33.833 --> 05:36.294
I'm Hogan of the Ministry of Science
Defense Agency.

05:37.003 --> 05:38.004
Nice to meet you.

05:39.088 --> 05:41.424
I've been assigned as your bodyguard.

05:41.924 --> 05:46.763
They say you're the next target
since Detective Gesicht has been killed.

05:46.846 --> 05:51.726
My power isn't even
in the same league as yours.

05:52.727 --> 05:54.479
But with all this rain

05:54.562 --> 05:56.898
and with you being powered
by Photon Energy...

05:58.858 --> 06:00.818
I'll take you to the safe house.

06:02.487 --> 06:04.697
But what about the children?

06:05.490 --> 06:07.825
We cannot drag them into this.

06:10.078 --> 06:11.913
Today is my birthday, you see.

06:12.830 --> 06:13.664
Huh?

06:14.374 --> 06:17.335
The children are throwing me a party.

06:19.253 --> 06:21.130
It's a surprise party.

06:21.798 --> 06:24.926
Well, it's meant to be a surprise,
but I already know about it.

06:27.345 --> 06:29.514
Can you make it short?

06:30.473 --> 06:31.349
Thank you.

06:43.820 --> 06:44.821
Oh, you all...

06:50.660 --> 06:52.412
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday!

06:52.495 --> 06:53.413
Thank you.

06:54.080 --> 06:55.623
Thank you very much, everyone!

06:56.124 --> 06:58.000
We have presents for you, Epsilon!

06:58.876 --> 07:01.629
Wow, really? I'm so happy!

07:02.171 --> 07:03.714
This is from us!

07:04.549 --> 07:05.675
What a lovely necklace!

07:06.467 --> 07:08.636
- You made this yourselves?
- Yes!

07:09.679 --> 07:11.097
This hat is lovely too.

07:11.597 --> 07:12.849
Look at that, Epsilon.

07:12.932 --> 07:15.184
It's something you love!

07:17.520 --> 07:18.438
It's the sun, huh?

07:18.521 --> 07:23.067
With this, you can feel happy
even on a rainy day like today, right?

07:23.693 --> 07:25.027
You're right. Amazing!

07:25.611 --> 07:26.654
It does cheer me up.

07:27.238 --> 07:30.825
See? I told you he would love it!

07:33.661 --> 07:36.581
These children
lost their parents in the war.

07:37.331 --> 07:39.292
To those kids,

07:40.001 --> 07:42.712
Epsilon is like their sun.

07:45.882 --> 07:48.759
Hey, Wassily, you drew something
for Epsilon, right?

07:49.260 --> 07:50.553
Don't be shy. Show him!

07:51.053 --> 07:51.888
Is that true?

07:52.805 --> 07:53.639
Let me see.

08:03.441 --> 08:04.567
Bora...

08:05.485 --> 08:07.278
This is Bora?

08:07.904 --> 08:09.322
Bora

08:10.656 --> 08:12.116
ate it...

08:12.950 --> 08:14.076
Earth...

08:14.160 --> 08:17.663
Wassily is saying something
other than "Bora"!

08:17.747 --> 08:18.789
...ate it...

08:20.458 --> 08:26.464
<i>The giant made a south pole
In the desert</i>

08:26.547 --> 08:27.548
A song?

08:27.632 --> 08:33.930
<i>The giant released a river of fire
And summoned the floating glaciers</i>

08:34.597 --> 08:41.187
<i>The giant made the rains come down
Until there was a great flood</i>

08:41.270 --> 08:47.777
<i>The giant swallowed the fire
The glaciers, and all the rain</i>

08:48.277 --> 08:51.739
<i>And then he ate</i>

08:53.533 --> 08:54.742
<i>The earth itself</i>

08:55.284 --> 08:58.579
<i>He ate</i>

09:00.414 --> 09:01.666
<i>The earth itself</i>

09:02.291 --> 09:04.210
Amazing, Wassily!

09:04.293 --> 09:05.419
But what a weird song!

09:10.508 --> 09:11.801
We need to get going.

09:12.885 --> 09:13.803
Five more minutes.

09:15.388 --> 09:17.098
It's been a while, Arnold.

09:17.598 --> 09:19.767
<i>Oh, why if it isn't Epsilon?</i>

09:20.351 --> 09:22.144
I'd like to ask you something.

09:22.728 --> 09:23.688
<i>Okay!</i>

09:23.771 --> 09:27.108
<i>Let the United States of Thracia's
best weather-forecasting robot, Arnold,</i>

09:27.191 --> 09:28.901
<i>predict it for you.</i>

09:28.985 --> 09:31.946
<i>The rain you've been having
should stop tomorrow before dawn.</i>

09:32.029 --> 09:32.947
<i>Just be patient--</i>

09:33.030 --> 09:34.031
Not that.

09:34.115 --> 09:35.157
Three years ago.

09:35.783 --> 09:37.368
<i>What? Three years ago?</i>

09:37.910 --> 09:39.537
Do you have any records

09:39.620 --> 09:42.373
of abnormal meteorological events
in Persia three years ago?

09:42.915 --> 09:45.585
For example, something like this picture.

09:46.711 --> 09:48.588
<i>What is that?</i>

09:49.130 --> 09:50.423
I'm not exactly sure.

09:51.507 --> 09:53.884
<i>Three years ago in Persia, huh?</i>

09:57.430 --> 09:58.973
<i>Nothing in particular.</i>

09:59.056 --> 10:01.183
<i>The smoke you see in this data</i>

10:01.767 --> 10:04.270
<i>is the kind caused
by battlefield artillery shells.</i>

10:04.979 --> 10:09.275
<i>Some of the children you took in
are from this area, aren't they?</i>

10:09.775 --> 10:11.360
- Yes.
- Huh?

10:13.362 --> 10:16.991
<i>There's something gigantic
inside the smoke...</i>

10:17.074 --> 10:18.242
What is it?

10:19.702 --> 10:21.746
<i>It's impossible to analyze.</i>

10:21.829 --> 10:23.080
It's time, sir.

10:27.460 --> 10:28.711
I'll be back soon.

10:29.211 --> 10:31.088
Epsilon, where are you going?

10:31.172 --> 10:33.424
What about the rest
of your birthday party?

10:34.467 --> 10:35.968
Some last-minute work came up.

10:38.220 --> 10:39.680
Be good while I'm gone, okay?

10:52.902 --> 10:53.986
Wassily...

10:55.237 --> 10:56.155
Wassily?

11:16.300 --> 11:17.259
Hey, over here.

11:25.184 --> 11:27.311
It's dark, so watch your step.

11:29.855 --> 11:32.900
I guess you do come in handy.

11:39.949 --> 11:41.867
Sir, I have brought him.

11:42.451 --> 11:45.788
Whoa, you're bright. Dim your light.

11:48.833 --> 11:51.252
I'm Brigadier General Scott
of the UN Forces.

11:51.335 --> 11:53.754
So you're the Epsilon
who refused to join the army.

11:55.756 --> 11:58.759
You've got a dainty frame for a robot.

11:59.301 --> 12:00.886
No wonder you're a coward.

12:01.512 --> 12:03.806
At least you can help
with the post-war cleanup.

12:04.306 --> 12:06.642
Have a look. This is your job.

12:09.687 --> 12:10.730
What is this?

12:12.106 --> 12:14.108
You are going to melt all of this down.

12:16.360 --> 12:19.488
With your Photon Energy,
you'll finish in no time, right?

12:21.073 --> 12:23.659
You want me to do that

12:24.577 --> 12:25.453
to these?

12:26.036 --> 12:29.665
They're advanced robots, but their
artificial intelligence has been removed.

12:30.374 --> 12:32.460
It's just a pile of marionettes.

12:33.252 --> 12:34.503
It can't be.

12:36.046 --> 12:40.551
I'd heard that the robot rights
had been recognized in Persia.

12:42.303 --> 12:44.430
What happened to the AI that was removed?

12:44.972 --> 12:45.890
No idea.

12:46.724 --> 12:48.851
Anyway, just get it done quickly.

12:49.810 --> 12:52.229
I'll let you know
when we're at a safe distance.

13:09.914 --> 13:11.332
<i>You ready, Epsilon?</i>

13:12.500 --> 13:14.752
<i>- I'll start the countdown.</i>
- Wait!

13:16.295 --> 13:19.423
<i>We're past the scheduled time.
Start the process immediately.</i>

13:19.507 --> 13:20.549
No, listen to me!

13:21.133 --> 13:23.260
- There's still someone nearby!
-<i>What?</i>

13:23.344 --> 13:24.345
Someone's out there.

13:24.428 --> 13:28.307
<i>That's impossible. We've checked.
There's no one left alive.</i>

13:28.390 --> 13:30.142
I'm getting a life-form reading.

13:30.226 --> 13:33.103
<i>Must be a dog or a cat. Just do your job.</i>

13:43.697 --> 13:44.532
Come here.

13:45.199 --> 13:46.033
It's okay.

13:47.576 --> 13:48.452
Don't be scared.

13:48.953 --> 13:49.787
Come on out.

13:54.250 --> 13:55.209
Here.

14:24.572 --> 14:26.866
Bora...

14:31.161 --> 14:34.039
Bora...

14:39.044 --> 14:40.838
Do you realize that you...

14:40.921 --> 14:42.047
No.

14:42.131 --> 14:44.550
I almost turned this boy to ashes!

14:44.633 --> 14:46.886
We'll take care of the kid.

14:48.596 --> 14:51.223
We don't have much time.
Just get on with it.

14:56.478 --> 14:59.189
<i>Eight, seven, six,</i>

14:59.273 --> 15:01.191
<i>five, four,</i>

15:01.275 --> 15:02.192
<i>three,</i>

15:02.276 --> 15:03.193
<i>two,</i>

15:03.277 --> 15:04.153
<i>one.</i>

15:24.882 --> 15:26.884
It's been a while, eh, Epsilon?

15:27.551 --> 15:31.764
It's me, Scott, from the UN Forces,
though now I'm a full general.

15:32.348 --> 15:34.600
Excellent work you did back then.

15:34.683 --> 15:36.602
Quite a flashy explosion, as I recall.

15:37.102 --> 15:40.439
Quite frankly, he's got so much power,

15:40.522 --> 15:43.442
it's silly for us to think
we can act as his protection.

15:46.612 --> 15:50.157
<i>Plus, this is more like a fortress
than a safe house.</i>

15:50.824 --> 15:54.703
<i>But of course, you are the last
of the most advanced robots.</i>

15:54.787 --> 15:57.873
<i>If anything happened to you,
it would be a loss for the whole planet.</i>

15:58.582 --> 16:00.751
I'm sure you know this already,

16:00.834 --> 16:03.504
but according to the data retrieved
from Detective Gesicht,

16:03.587 --> 16:04.964
the enemy's name is--

16:05.047 --> 16:05.923
Pluto.

16:06.006 --> 16:06.840
Right.

16:08.092 --> 16:09.176
<i>And as his brain,</i>

16:10.177 --> 16:13.389
<i>the AI of another robot named Sahad
had been installed.</i>

16:15.099 --> 16:16.558
You're prepared as expected.

16:17.643 --> 16:19.228
What is Bora?

16:20.938 --> 16:23.107
Those robot corpses I destroyed...

16:24.233 --> 16:25.818
How are they connected to Bora?

16:26.652 --> 16:27.653
"Connected"?

16:28.529 --> 16:31.657
What was the Bora Inquiry Commission
in the first place?

16:32.157 --> 16:35.244
The members of that mission
who found that robot graveyard

16:35.327 --> 16:37.287
are being killed off one by one.

16:37.955 --> 16:39.957
Now is not the time for secrets!

16:40.040 --> 16:41.667
Your life is in danger too!

16:42.918 --> 16:45.379
Pluto's power is terrifying.

16:46.422 --> 16:50.259
But an even greater power
is waiting beyond its evolution.

16:51.635 --> 16:52.720
One that could

16:54.471 --> 16:56.682
"eat the earth itself."

16:57.391 --> 16:59.226
What are you talking about?

16:59.810 --> 17:02.271
It's from the song
that boy was singing, isn't it?

17:03.439 --> 17:05.649
Listen, they're singing it even now.

17:07.693 --> 17:09.737
Yes, I can hear it.

17:10.988 --> 17:16.702
<i>The giant made a south pole in the desert</i>

17:16.785 --> 17:22.583
<i>The giant released a river of fire
And summoned the floating glaciers</i>

17:22.666 --> 17:28.464
<i>The giant made the rains come down
Until there was a great flood</i>

17:28.547 --> 17:34.303
<i>The giant swallowed the fire
The glaciers, and all the rain</i>

17:34.386 --> 17:40.142
<i>And then he ate up the whole earth!</i>

17:40.225 --> 17:45.689
<i>And he ate up the whole earth!</i>

17:45.773 --> 17:48.609
<i>Bora</i>

17:48.692 --> 17:51.403
<i>Bora</i>

17:51.487 --> 17:54.448
<i>Bora</i>

17:54.531 --> 17:57.409
<i>Bora</i>

17:57.493 --> 18:00.746
<i>Bora</i>

18:00.829 --> 18:04.875
Hey, Wassily. Everyone loves your song.

18:12.049 --> 18:16.845
<i>The giant made the rains come down
Until there was a great flood</i>

18:16.929 --> 18:21.975
<i>The giant ate up the fire
The glacier, and all the rain</i>

18:22.059 --> 18:26.480
<i>And then he ate the earth itself!</i>

18:26.563 --> 18:28.982
<i>Bora</i>

18:29.066 --> 18:31.276
<i>Bora...</i>

18:31.360 --> 18:33.070
What's the matter, Deacon?

18:36.990 --> 18:39.451
- What's going on?
- What is it?

18:44.998 --> 18:47.042
No! They have to flee!

18:47.126 --> 18:48.335
Flee?

18:48.418 --> 18:49.253
What's wrong?

18:50.087 --> 18:52.673
I must return to Australia right away!

18:53.924 --> 18:55.134
Oh, wow.

18:55.968 --> 18:57.136
What is that?

19:02.975 --> 19:04.560
Everyone, run!

19:06.145 --> 19:07.813
There's something above us too?

19:08.397 --> 19:10.983
General, take your men and run!

19:11.066 --> 19:16.530
Run? The defense system here
can instantly respond to any attack.

19:16.613 --> 19:20.200
We aren't like you,
who only thinks about running away.

19:20.826 --> 19:22.035
You have to flee n--

19:27.457 --> 19:28.417
Epsilon!

19:28.500 --> 19:31.003
Do you read me, Epsilon?

19:34.673 --> 19:36.049
I have to save them!

19:36.550 --> 19:39.887
It's too late. Everyone's been vaporized.

19:41.263 --> 19:43.473
Because of me, they all...

19:44.224 --> 19:45.058
That's not true!

19:45.976 --> 19:49.771
There were plenty of chances to target you
over the last three months.

19:50.272 --> 19:52.774
It's highly possible
that the general was the target.

19:53.609 --> 19:55.819
The Bora Inquiry Commission assassinations...

19:56.320 --> 19:57.279
Take a look.

20:04.786 --> 20:06.413
They look like two horns.

20:12.044 --> 20:14.796
Whatever the case,
I must return to the children!

20:17.841 --> 20:19.843
Such destructive power.

20:20.886 --> 20:22.429
What weapon could do this?

20:23.889 --> 20:24.723
No.

20:25.265 --> 20:26.099
It was probably

20:27.267 --> 20:28.227
Bora.

20:29.019 --> 20:30.270
What is Bora?

20:31.688 --> 20:32.564
I'm not sure.

20:33.815 --> 20:36.526
It's like he has emotions
but doesn't at the same time.

20:39.738 --> 20:41.531
Is he just a puppet?

20:44.660 --> 20:45.661
Who is it?

20:45.744 --> 20:48.747
Who? Just take a look.

20:48.830 --> 20:51.959
It's me. Higeoyaji.

20:52.542 --> 20:53.877
Oh, Principal Ban.

20:55.379 --> 20:56.922
I wasn't asking about you.

20:57.422 --> 20:59.675
Then what did you mean?

21:00.425 --> 21:06.473
I just saw two great rushes of sadness
emerge somewhere in the world.

21:10.060 --> 21:11.603
<i>Pinocchio,</i> eh?

21:12.729 --> 21:16.275
<i>Pinocchio struggled to learn
about the human heart.</i>

21:16.900 --> 21:17.859
<i>But Uran,</i>

21:17.943 --> 21:22.197
you have more heart than most humans.

21:24.408 --> 21:25.409
They're crying.

21:26.410 --> 21:27.452
What's the matter?

21:27.953 --> 21:28.787
You can tell me.

21:32.040 --> 21:34.001
Why are you crying so much?

21:36.712 --> 21:37.921
Wow!

21:38.005 --> 21:39.298
It's coming this way.

21:39.881 --> 21:41.633
Should we run?

21:42.134 --> 21:44.720
I'm sure we'll be fine
if we stay inside the house.

22:22.924 --> 22:25.093
Everyone! Gather around me!

22:25.844 --> 22:26.720
Now!

22:30.807 --> 22:31.767
Huddle closer!

22:34.144 --> 22:36.438
Get down and protect your heads!

22:41.151 --> 22:42.319
Epsilon!

22:52.704 --> 22:53.622
Get down!

23:03.799 --> 23:04.758
It's okay.

23:06.051 --> 23:06.927
Don't be scared.

23:08.762 --> 23:09.679
Come on out.

23:11.056 --> 23:11.932
Here.

23:28.407 --> 23:29.241
What power...

23:39.876 --> 23:41.586
The sun came out.

23:43.463 --> 23:44.297
Hey, look!

23:45.382 --> 23:47.801
There are two suns!

24:10.949 --> 24:12.784
Epsilon!

24:20.584 --> 24:21.585
Thank goodness.

24:22.169 --> 24:23.795
You defeated it, then?

24:29.843 --> 24:30.677
Wassily...

24:32.929 --> 24:35.182
Epsilon...

24:36.558 --> 24:40.604
You called my name for the first time.

24:43.231 --> 24:45.567
Thank you.

24:48.695 --> 24:49.988
Thank you,

24:51.281 --> 24:52.616
Epsilon.

25:10.258 --> 25:11.134
Uran.

25:11.927 --> 25:12.761
Uran!

25:13.303 --> 25:14.387
What's wrong?

25:16.056 --> 25:17.140
He's Pinocchio.

25:18.141 --> 25:18.975
What?

25:19.976 --> 25:21.353
The child is like Pinocchio.

25:22.270 --> 25:24.689
The one who was sad and crying?

25:26.149 --> 25:27.234
He can't find it.

25:28.360 --> 25:29.194
His heart.

25:32.364 --> 25:33.740
<i>No matter where he goes,</i>

25:34.241 --> 25:36.493
<i>it's darker than inside the whale's belly.</i>

25:37.619 --> 25:39.246
He doesn't want to be a puppet.

25:39.955 --> 25:41.581
He doesn't want to be controlled.

25:42.749 --> 25:44.876
He thinks he's acting on his own,

25:46.503 --> 25:48.380
but he's controlled by his hatred.

25:50.382 --> 25:53.885
But you see,
he's not the only one being controlled.

25:55.929 --> 25:57.055
<i>Geppetto is too.</i>

25:59.474 --> 26:00.725
Geppetto is

26:01.393 --> 26:03.186
just another puppet.

26:05.981 --> 26:08.024
I wanted to talk to him some more.

26:11.486 --> 26:12.529
But he's gone.

26:25.417 --> 26:30.839
Can you tell them to hold off
on Atom's state funeral?

26:31.423 --> 26:33.633
<i>If that's what you'd like, sure...</i>

26:34.175 --> 26:35.010
Thank you.

26:49.524 --> 26:54.446
Come on, Wassily!
Run faster, or you're gonna get tagged!

26:56.031 --> 26:56.906
You're it!

27:04.205 --> 27:06.541
Are you all right, Wassily?

27:06.625 --> 27:08.001
Oh, someone is coming.

27:13.131 --> 27:14.424
It's Mr. Simon.

27:15.884 --> 27:19.220
Hello there. Nice weather today, eh?

27:19.304 --> 27:21.681
It sure is.

27:24.059 --> 27:25.602
Is Epsilon around?

27:26.227 --> 27:27.646
Unfortunately, no.

27:28.313 --> 27:30.357
Oh, he's not here?

27:30.440 --> 27:32.359
He's not. He's at a hearing.

27:33.068 --> 27:34.235
A hearing?

27:37.530 --> 27:39.240
So, Epsilon,

27:40.408 --> 27:42.786
did you defeat your adversary?

27:43.453 --> 27:44.412
Yes, I did.

27:44.496 --> 27:45.580
Are you sure?

27:46.122 --> 27:48.333
I thought robots couldn't tell lies.

27:48.917 --> 27:50.543
I defeated my enemy.

27:51.086 --> 27:52.962
Completely?

27:54.631 --> 27:56.549
I defeated my enemy.

27:57.258 --> 27:59.219
Then can we discuss the other issue?

27:59.302 --> 28:01.638
Why did you fail to protect the general?

28:02.138 --> 28:06.559
Everyone stationed at the safe house
was gone in an instant.

28:08.061 --> 28:09.187
That was different.

28:10.021 --> 28:12.107
It was an attack with a different weapon.

28:12.607 --> 28:14.025
A different weapon?

28:15.985 --> 28:18.488
In any case, please take a look at these.

28:19.906 --> 28:23.368
These are the parts scattered
around Epsilon's orphanage.

28:24.285 --> 28:27.288
They seem to be from the left arm
of a robot made in Persia.

28:27.372 --> 28:28.790
A robot that was created

28:28.873 --> 28:32.085
for environmental development
but converted for the military.

28:32.168 --> 28:33.586
Just the left arm?

28:34.087 --> 28:35.004
Anything else?

28:35.672 --> 28:37.173
Not that we have found.

28:37.841 --> 28:41.845
Epsilon, we're all aware
of your pacifist views,

28:42.429 --> 28:47.308
so we're concerned that you may have
gone easy on the enemy again.

28:53.523 --> 28:57.402
No matter how many times we fight,
he will never be my adversary.

28:58.778 --> 29:02.991
Something like this should be discussed
once Epsilon gets back.

29:03.074 --> 29:04.909
That's why I came today.

29:05.535 --> 29:06.369
What?

29:06.453 --> 29:09.122
I'm sure you are aware, Ms. Griffith,

29:09.664 --> 29:12.667
of what people say about this foster home,

29:13.585 --> 29:16.838
about whether a robot
can be a parent to a human child.

29:17.797 --> 29:19.924
We at the Child Services Agency

29:20.425 --> 29:24.804
have no problem with outstanding humans
like you serving as childcare workers.

29:26.181 --> 29:28.683
The problem is Epsilon.

29:30.018 --> 29:33.772
Epsilon cares more for the children
than any human could!

29:34.481 --> 29:36.065
Even so,

29:36.149 --> 29:40.361
it would be better for these children
to be taken in by humans.

29:40.945 --> 29:41.905
Don't you agree?

29:44.574 --> 29:50.747
Especially since we have Mr. Johansen here
willing to get involved.

29:50.830 --> 29:51.664
Yes.

29:52.165 --> 29:56.044
Once he becomes my child,
I will make sure he has a happy life.

29:56.628 --> 30:00.507
Mr. Johansen is one
of the most prominent people in Oslo.

30:01.257 --> 30:04.552
My wife and I have visited several times,
and our hearts are set

30:04.636 --> 30:06.179
on helping this child.

30:06.679 --> 30:08.598
I hope for a favorable answer.

30:10.558 --> 30:11.434
But

30:12.977 --> 30:15.688
out of all the children, why that boy?

30:19.400 --> 30:20.401
Yes?

30:21.402 --> 30:22.320
I've brought him.

30:23.696 --> 30:24.697
Oh!

30:31.621 --> 30:34.624
Wassily, come here.

30:37.168 --> 30:38.378
Wassily.

30:42.632 --> 30:44.884
It's okay. Don't be scared.

30:45.885 --> 30:47.971
Wassily, have you ever seen snow before?

30:50.515 --> 30:53.309
Mr. Johansen, Wassily is--

30:53.393 --> 30:57.981
Mr. Johansen is prepared to make
a substantial donation to the foster home.

30:59.274 --> 31:01.818
Are you going to deny the boy the chance

31:01.901 --> 31:06.155
to be adopted by ideal parents
just because he doesn't like it?

31:07.198 --> 31:09.409
Why don't we go see snow?

31:17.375 --> 31:18.960
Look! It's Epsilon!

31:22.672 --> 31:25.675
- Welcome back, Epsilon!
- It's Epsilon!

31:25.758 --> 31:26.968
Welcome, Epsilon!

31:27.051 --> 31:27.927
You're back!

31:28.011 --> 31:30.555
Hey now, I've only got one body, you know.

31:31.180 --> 31:34.017
Stop that, children.
Epsilon must be tired.

31:34.642 --> 31:36.853
The hearing must have been tough.

31:37.395 --> 31:38.229
It was fine.

31:39.022 --> 31:41.441
Well then, what shall we play today?

31:46.571 --> 31:47.405
Where's Wassily?

31:48.239 --> 31:49.782
He went with that man.

31:50.283 --> 31:52.118
The man who's really rich.

31:52.744 --> 31:53.620
What's going on?

31:56.414 --> 31:58.791
Where's Wassily?

32:00.168 --> 32:01.002
He went to Oslo.

32:02.003 --> 32:04.631
Oslo? No one told me about this!

32:06.507 --> 32:08.426
We had no choice.

32:24.734 --> 32:26.194
Enough already.

32:27.779 --> 32:30.156
How many times do you have to stop?

32:32.200 --> 32:37.080
Mr. Johansen is prepared to make
a substantial donation to the foster home.

32:48.508 --> 32:50.551
There's no point holding hands anymore!

32:52.136 --> 32:53.262
There's the door.

32:53.346 --> 32:55.515
Once you go through, my work is done.

32:56.307 --> 32:58.476
Don't give me any more trouble.
Quickly now.

33:00.353 --> 33:02.105
I told you to hurry up!

33:05.024 --> 33:06.567
I have the tracking results!

33:08.236 --> 33:11.614
Wassily was taken
to Vigeland Castle in Oslo.

33:12.365 --> 33:13.199
However,

33:14.200 --> 33:18.079
Johansen, the man who took Wassily,
doesn't exist.

33:18.663 --> 33:19.872
- What--
- That can't be.

33:23.334 --> 33:24.502
I've brought the boy.

33:34.887 --> 33:37.390
I hope you've been gentle with him.

33:37.473 --> 33:41.144
Why, I handled him
as if he were made of glass.

33:44.939 --> 33:46.816
Well then, if you'd excuse me...

33:56.784 --> 33:57.910
Bora...

34:00.872 --> 34:02.373
Don't be scared.

34:02.457 --> 34:07.712
Bora!

34:07.795 --> 34:09.881
Don't worry. Everything's fine.

34:10.506 --> 34:13.301
- There's nothing to be scared of.
- Bora!

34:13.384 --> 34:16.929
You'd better not shout that so loud.

34:17.847 --> 34:21.392
You're a bad boy.
That's why this is happening to you.

34:22.060 --> 34:24.854
You're a very bad boy for seeing Bora.

34:27.398 --> 34:31.277
But Epsilon will come to the rescue,
even for a bad boy like you.

34:31.360 --> 34:34.280
Epsilon is quite kind, isn't he?

34:35.239 --> 34:36.240
Isn't that right?

34:56.177 --> 34:58.054
I've come this far for you.

34:58.763 --> 35:00.932
Failure is not an option. Not this time.

35:02.975 --> 35:07.647
Epsilon is the last one remaining.
Kill him, and all will be over.

35:09.357 --> 35:10.775
You will be victorious.

35:11.275 --> 35:14.904
Even with only one arm, you will win.

35:16.030 --> 35:18.032
When it's all over,

35:19.492 --> 35:22.787
the world will regret
the sins it has committed!

35:23.746 --> 35:24.997
You hear me, Pluto?

35:40.012 --> 35:41.430
Epsilon, isn't that...

35:41.973 --> 35:45.518
The body armor that was issued to me
during the Central Asian War.

35:46.352 --> 35:49.313
I had no need for it
since I refused to enlist.

35:49.397 --> 35:50.356
Wait!

35:51.816 --> 35:53.860
Wassily's life is in danger.

35:53.943 --> 35:56.737
The military will be ready to deploy
any moment now.

35:57.321 --> 35:58.865
It's me they're after.

36:00.324 --> 36:03.369
Why didn't you finish him off?

36:07.081 --> 36:11.169
You must have had the chance
to strike the final blow.

36:11.836 --> 36:13.713
Why didn't you do it?

36:24.849 --> 36:28.436
You don't need to come.
I don't want to create any more victims.

36:29.020 --> 36:30.271
No, I'm coming with you.

36:30.354 --> 36:32.273
You don't need to protect me.

36:32.857 --> 36:35.026
I'll be protecting Wassily.

36:59.508 --> 37:01.928
He'll be here any moment, Pluto.

37:04.972 --> 37:06.766
You must settle it by sunrise.

37:11.604 --> 37:13.898
Bora!

37:13.981 --> 37:15.566
Be quiet!

37:23.950 --> 37:25.284
What are you doing?

37:28.704 --> 37:30.414
Defying your father, are you?

37:32.458 --> 37:36.504
Since when do you take
that sort of attitude with your creator?

37:38.547 --> 37:43.678
Once this battle is over,
you can go back to your original body.

37:47.306 --> 37:49.600
You know that, right, Pluto?

38:00.611 --> 38:02.697
I'm picking up Wassily's bio-readings.

38:03.239 --> 38:04.407
I'm going in.

38:04.490 --> 38:05.992
I want you to stay here.

38:06.075 --> 38:08.536
<i>But you are a Photon Energy-powered robot.</i>

38:08.619 --> 38:09.996
<i>You should wait until sunrise!</i>

38:10.079 --> 38:12.957
I have to rescue Wassily
as soon as possible!

38:13.708 --> 38:16.085
<i>Wait! I will use my stealth ability!</i>

38:32.059 --> 38:32.893
Behind this door.

38:35.479 --> 38:36.564
I'll break it down.

38:38.441 --> 38:39.358
Breach!

38:44.155 --> 38:45.281
Epsilon!

38:45.364 --> 38:46.782
Rescue Wassily, quickly!

38:46.866 --> 38:48.200
- But--
- Hurry!

38:48.826 --> 38:49.660
Wassily!

38:56.292 --> 38:58.169
He still had that much power left?

39:07.053 --> 39:09.805
Wassily! Are you all right? Wassily!

39:18.689 --> 39:20.232
I'm running out of energy.

39:21.067 --> 39:22.193
Is it

39:23.110 --> 39:24.028
dawn yet?

39:35.539 --> 39:38.876
Finish him! Finish him off, Pluto!

39:47.218 --> 39:50.096
The child...

39:50.846 --> 39:51.972
The child?

39:52.640 --> 39:53.808
You mean Wassily?

39:53.891 --> 39:58.270
I've secured Wassily! He is safe, Epsilon!

39:59.188 --> 40:00.731
He's safe!

40:04.276 --> 40:07.321
Is it Sahad inside you?

40:09.490 --> 40:11.117
What happened to you?

40:12.118 --> 40:13.411
Who is Abullah?

40:14.120 --> 40:15.329
What is Bora?

40:19.125 --> 40:20.209
The sun is rising.

40:21.335 --> 40:23.212
Finish him off now!

40:30.970 --> 40:34.890
Help...

40:36.392 --> 40:40.980
Help me...

40:59.790 --> 41:01.709
TOBIO TENMA

41:05.212 --> 41:06.672
So it was you.

41:07.673 --> 41:11.302
You're the one who's been leaving flowers
at Tobio's grave.

41:12.511 --> 41:13.512
You're...

41:16.807 --> 41:18.684
This is my son's grave.

41:22.688 --> 41:24.315
Are you, by any chance...

41:25.399 --> 41:26.484
I'm Uran.

41:26.567 --> 41:29.028
Atom's little sister.

41:29.111 --> 41:30.112
Yes.

41:33.073 --> 41:35.201
A robot visiting a grave...

41:35.784 --> 41:37.328
Truly incredible.

41:37.953 --> 41:40.247
You're Ochanomizu's masterpiece.

41:41.790 --> 41:43.292
Can you tell me

41:43.959 --> 41:46.754
how Tobio is doing up in heaven?

41:48.130 --> 41:50.591
I don't know about heaven
or that sort of thing,

41:51.300 --> 41:55.262
but I do know that you are grieving.

41:56.931 --> 41:58.182
You do?

41:58.891 --> 42:01.435
You understand grief?
Understand the heart?

42:02.770 --> 42:05.523
I don't know if it can be called a heart,
but emotions...

42:06.565 --> 42:08.400
Like right now.

42:10.819 --> 42:12.446
Somewhere, far away,

42:13.656 --> 42:14.990
I sense two emotions.

42:16.200 --> 42:18.786
Terrible, terrible sadness...

42:20.913 --> 42:21.914
<i>from two sources.</i>

42:25.501 --> 42:26.335
It's sunrise!

42:26.418 --> 42:27.878
You've won, Epsilon!

42:27.962 --> 42:30.339
What are you doing? Finish him off, Pluto!

42:31.966 --> 42:37.888
Why didn't you finish me off last time?

42:38.931 --> 42:42.309
Why didn't you kill me?

42:42.393 --> 42:46.272
Because the wavelengths you emit told me...

42:50.317 --> 42:51.694
you were sad.

42:52.278 --> 42:56.448
Then kill me now!

43:11.880 --> 43:14.675
That's it.

43:15.259 --> 43:19.847
Use your Photon Energy to melt me away!

43:21.807 --> 43:25.185
Do it! Kill me, please!

43:27.229 --> 43:30.107
Come on! Do it!

43:49.168 --> 43:50.377
You are

43:51.879 --> 43:53.130
Sahad.

43:57.217 --> 43:58.969
Let's find your original body.

43:59.637 --> 44:03.974
We'll put your artificial intelligence
back into your original body.

44:04.600 --> 44:05.434
Let's stop this.

44:08.228 --> 44:09.897
You can stop by your own will.

44:14.818 --> 44:15.653
I can't.

44:18.447 --> 44:19.823
He's coming.

44:21.367 --> 44:22.534
Who's coming?

44:27.706 --> 44:31.335
The sun. It should have risen already,

44:32.586 --> 44:33.671
yet it's disappeared.

44:38.175 --> 44:39.593
Bora!

44:42.763 --> 44:44.223
What's happening?

44:44.723 --> 44:46.100
Wassily!

44:46.725 --> 44:49.853
It's no use! I can't hold on!

44:50.896 --> 44:54.024
Use my energy!

45:07.287 --> 45:08.372
Epsilon...

45:19.633 --> 45:21.343
That's your brother.

45:29.810 --> 45:31.812
Dr. Tenma? Doctor?

45:34.106 --> 45:35.983
Wassily! Are you all right?

45:36.567 --> 45:38.444
Your hands are protecting us!

45:54.710 --> 45:56.462
<i>Hi, everyone.</i>

45:58.380 --> 46:00.549
<i>Everyone, I'm back.</i>

46:02.593 --> 46:03.594
<i>What's going on?</i>

46:04.553 --> 46:05.471
<i>Everyone?</i>

46:07.264 --> 46:08.223
<i>I see.</i>

46:09.183 --> 46:10.976
<i>This is just an image in my memory.</i>

46:12.394 --> 46:17.024
<i>I thought you all were here in real life,
so I tried to hug you.</i>

46:19.359 --> 46:20.527
<i>Hug you...</i>

46:23.113 --> 46:23.989
<i>Huh?</i>

46:26.283 --> 46:27.493
<i>Where are my arms?</i>

46:31.038 --> 46:32.372
<i>Where is my body?</i>

46:35.959 --> 46:37.169
<i>Am I...</i>

46:52.976 --> 46:53.811
Atom?

46:54.812 --> 46:57.439
Do you recognize me, Atom? It's me, Uran!

46:58.982 --> 47:00.859
<i>So he's finally awakened.</i>

47:02.402 --> 47:03.695
Dr. Tenma.

47:04.238 --> 47:07.533
<i>I've installed certain data
in his artificial intelligence.</i>

47:08.116 --> 47:09.910
<i>Unbalanced emotions.</i>

47:10.410 --> 47:13.330
<i>A program to simplify the chaos.</i>

47:14.164 --> 47:17.292
<i>It finished processing
all the information,</i>

47:17.376 --> 47:20.504
and the only thing left to do
was to wait for him to wake up.

47:20.587 --> 47:21.880
And now, it has finally--

47:25.133 --> 47:26.760
What are these brain waves?

47:27.511 --> 47:28.929
And these numbers?

47:31.473 --> 47:33.517
What is going on here?

47:34.351 --> 47:36.311
<i>Something came down just now.</i>

47:36.937 --> 47:39.064
Right before Atom opened his eyes,

47:39.815 --> 47:41.066
something flew down!

47:41.650 --> 47:43.026
What is this "something"?

47:45.571 --> 47:47.364
A humongous

47:48.782 --> 47:49.616
sadness.

47:51.410 --> 47:52.411
<i>I understand now.</i>

47:53.078 --> 47:54.496
<i>I understand everything.</i>

47:55.497 --> 47:56.540
<i>I know who Pluto is,</i>

47:57.666 --> 47:58.959
<i>who Abullah is,</i>

47:59.793 --> 48:02.462
<i>and what Bora is.</i>

48:17.519 --> 48:20.439
Bora!

48:21.023 --> 48:22.316
That huge shadow...

48:23.191 --> 48:24.359
Is that Bora?

48:25.611 --> 48:28.697
Epsilon is...

48:28.780 --> 48:29.948
Don't look!

48:30.032 --> 48:30.866
Epsilon...

48:31.617 --> 48:32.492
Epsilon has...

48:34.620 --> 48:36.079
become light.

48:45.589 --> 48:47.049
The morning sun is back.

48:48.175 --> 48:51.428
The giant shadow is gone, and so is Pluto.

48:52.429 --> 48:53.347
Those hands...

48:54.806 --> 48:56.183
Epsilon's hands!

48:56.850 --> 48:57.684
Yes.

48:58.352 --> 49:00.062
They protected us.

49:15.535 --> 49:17.704
Thank you, Epsilon.

49:22.042 --> 49:22.876
<i>Someone.</i>

49:25.671 --> 49:26.505
<i>Anyone.</i>

49:27.339 --> 49:28.632
<i>Please, in my stead...</i>

49:31.843 --> 49:34.096
For the earth, in my stead...

49:36.890 --> 49:37.849
<i>For the earth...</i>

49:53.365 --> 49:54.282
Epsilon.

49:55.075 --> 50:00.288
You probably would be reluctant
to hear this,

50:01.832 --> 50:05.961
but you are no coward
who dodged enlistment.

50:07.337 --> 50:09.506
You were a truly brave warrior.

50:17.973 --> 50:21.351
Sadness flew down, huh?

50:22.019 --> 50:25.188
<i>Uran, you must love reading books.</i>

50:25.814 --> 50:26.648
What?

50:27.232 --> 50:31.236
You are simply good at
expressing things poetically.

50:31.903 --> 50:33.905
You don't understand
other people's feelings.

50:34.489 --> 50:36.616
But I do understand!

50:37.617 --> 50:41.580
<i>I know how sad you were
in front of Tobio's grave!</i>

50:42.664 --> 50:43.540
I sensed it!

50:44.583 --> 50:47.919
<i>I can sense how sad and empty
you feel right now!</i>

50:51.298 --> 50:52.924
Dr. Tenma, wait!

50:53.633 --> 50:54.801
Dr. Tenma!

51:00.098 --> 51:00.932
Atom.

51:01.516 --> 51:03.727
Atom, it's me, Uran! Do you understand me?

51:04.478 --> 51:05.437
I understand.

51:05.520 --> 51:06.938
Thank goodness.

51:07.564 --> 51:08.648
Atom,

51:09.316 --> 51:10.817
you came back to life.

51:12.277 --> 51:14.529
I understand, Epsilon.

51:15.155 --> 51:15.989
What?

51:17.074 --> 51:18.075
Atom?

51:18.825 --> 51:19.910
I understand,

51:21.411 --> 51:22.412
Gesicht.

51:29.961 --> 51:30.962
Hmm?

51:32.172 --> 51:33.256
A crack?

51:34.800 --> 51:36.718
The earth is going to break.

54:07.202 --> 54:10.872
Subtitle translation by: Astrid Oliver
